## Credential handling (NO SECRETS IN CODE OR GIT, EVER)

A credential is NEVER written in code and NEVER committed — in any form, at any time.
Always read from environment variables at runtime. `.env.example` carries placeholders
only. Test-only secrets live in test config, never in source. If you find a secret in a
diff or history, STOP and escalate — it must be rotated, not just deleted.

